/* book exam traps: Putting the water peak at 1550 nm. Its strongest overtone is near 1383 nm; the fundamental is at 2.73 µm. | Calling OH⁻ or metal-ion bands intrinsic. Intrinsic means the silica network itself; impurities are extrinsic. | Treating the whole 1300 to 1500 nm range as unusable. The water peak is a band a few tens of nm wide, and low-water-peak fiber removes most of it. | Blaming absorption for the 1550 nm loss floor. At 1550 nm Rayleigh scattering is the larger part; the infrared tail takes over only beyond about 1.6 µm. */
